NAME
    sticky - a sticky note for the desktop

SYNOPSIS
    sticky

DESCRIPTION
    A window holding one note. Type into it and it is kept: the text is
    written to /root/.sticky-note within a second of the last change, and
    again when the window is closed, so opening the note again - or
    restarting the whole desktop - gives back what was last written
    rather than an empty page.

    The status line names the file the note lives in and says whether it
    has been written, so a note that is still only in the window cannot
    be mistaken for one that is on disk.

    The editor is the small one a note needs: printable keys, Enter,
    Backspace, Delete, the arrows, Home and End. A row that reaches the
    right margin does not wrap, so a long line is scrolled sideways to
    keep the caret on screen, and a note longer than the window is
    scrolled vertically to keep the row being edited in view.

KEYS
    printable keys  type into the note
    Enter            start a new line
    Backspace        delete backwards, joining lines at the start
    Delete           delete forwards
    Arrows, Home, End  move the caret
    a click          put the caret where it landed
    Esc              save if needed and close the window

    The two buttons under the note save it at once and empty it.

FILES
    /root/.sticky-note  the note itself, rewritten as it changes

    Like the rest of the RAM filesystem that file is gone at reboot,
    where the desktop comes back with an empty note.
